{
  // Solution-style index of this repo's npm/TypeScript projects: packages/*,
  // apps/*, and makecode/simx/*. No build reads this file: tsc is always
  // invoked with an explicit project or from a package directory, and the
  // build driver runs per-package scripts.
  //
  // It exists for the EDITOR. Spec files are excluded from every project's
  // build config (they must not enter build programs), so without an
  // ancestor config referencing the tsconfig.spec.json projects, tsserver
  // assigns opened spec files to an inferred project and shows bogus
  // diagnostics. tsserver walks ancestor directories until a config owns
  // the file, then searches these references for the owning project.
  //
  // Keep the pairing per project: the build config, then its spec config.
  // The build-config entries make this an honest index of the repo; the
  // spec-config entries are the load-bearing ones. scripts/
  // editor-projects.spec.js enforces that every tsconfig.spec.json under
  // packages/, apps/, and makecode/simx/ is editor-reachable -- from here,
  // or from a tsconfig.json inside its own project -- run it (root
  // `npm test`) after config changes.
  //
  // makecode/simx/wendoo is absent deliberately: it is post-processed, and
  // no config outside it may reference into it (the post-processed-
  // references guard in external/wendoo-lang/packages/assistant-bridge).
  // Its own solution-style tsconfig.json indexes its entry and spec projects,
  // which the editor's nearest-config walk finds first anyway.
  //
  // makecode/extensions/** and makecode/tests/** are excluded by decision
  // and must never be indexed here. Their tsconfigs follow the pxt
  // editor-typing discipline (target ES5, noLib, ignoreDeprecations "6.0"),
  // are checkable only under typescript@6, and are served by tsserver's
  // nearest-config walk from their own directories.
  //
  // ORDERING CONSTRAINT: the editor assigns a file to the FIRST listed
  // project that contains it, so a project whose sources another project's
  // spec config includes must list its own configs BEFORE the including
  // project. The editor-projects gate asserts ownership and fails if this
  // order regresses.
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./packages/protocol/tsconfig.json" },
    { "path": "./packages/protocol/tsconfig.spec.json" },
    { "path": "./apps/bridge/tsconfig.json" },
    { "path": "./apps/bridge/tsconfig.spec.json" }
  ]
}
